t for percentages) Product revenues | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ B2C | | 357,975 | | 2.4 | | 261,197 | | 1.8 | | 223,217 | | 31,920 | | 1.8 B2B | | 14,483,935 | | 96.9 | | 14,033,543 | | 97.5 | | 12,247,430 | | 1,751,359 | | 97.5 Sub total | | 14,841,910 | | 99.3 | | 14,294,740 | | 99.3 | | 12,470,647 | | 1,783,279 | | 99.3 Service revenues | | 106,219 | | 0.7 | | 106,509 | | 0.7 | | 85,376 | | 12,209 | | 0.7 Total | | 14,948,129 | | 100.0 | | 14,401,249 | | 100.0 | | 12,556,023 | | 1,795,488 | | 100.0","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":1037,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"920e498710e4be24cff84e9636c68c1703dd0d21c999fdf0498d90628d7fdb2c","quote":"Service revenues. Service revenues primarily consist of marketplace (MP) service fees we charge to marketplace sellers to which we provide access to 1 Medicine Marketplace where they are able to effectively sell their products. We charge marketplace sellers commission fees equal to an agreed percentage of the sales price of the product when a sale is completed and also charge marketplace sellers an annual non-refundable up-front fee for platform usage. We refer to these fees as MP service revenue. Since we launched our MP service, it has made substantial contribution to our service revenues. We also generate service revenues by providing other ancillary services, mainly online medical consultation services for patients and digital marketing services for pharmaceutical companies.","context":"Product revenues. We historically reported our product revenues under our direct sales model from two reportable segments: the B2C segment and the B2B segment. Product revenues from our B2C segment are generated from the sale of pharmaceutical and other health and wellness products through 1 Medicine Marketplace, mobile apps and other online channels to consumers and certain enterprise customers. We also generate product revenues from the B2B segment through the sale of pharmaceutical products to pharmacies on 1 Pharmacy.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":1038,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"eedadfbb24d5ab069d7db98e8177c08ee41d715ef45f252f0c26ca708754b981","quote":"95","context":"Service revenues. Service revenues primarily consist of marketplace (MP) service fees we charge to marketplace sellers to which we provide access to 1 Medicine Marketplace where they are able to effectively sell their products. We charge marketplace sellers commission fees equal to an agreed percentage of the sales price of the product when a sale is completed and also charge marketplace sellers an annual non-refundable up-front fee for platform usage. We refer to these fees as MP service revenue. Since we launched our MP service, it has made substantial contribution to our service revenues. We also generate service revenues by providing other ancillary services, mainly online medical consultation services for patients and digital marketing services for pharmaceutical companies.","section":"Key Components of Results of Operations","block":1039,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"be69868769782019e305079d7c339de96c2fec192b2ef0af015c66c016e677ab","quote":"Product Revenues by Segment. Product revenues decreased by 12.8% from RMB14.3 billion in 2024 to RMB12.5 billion (US$1.8 billion) in 2025, as a result of (i) the 12.7% decrease in product revenue from B2B segment to RMB12.2 billion (US$1.7 billion) in 2025 from RMB14.0 billion in the prior year and (ii) the 14.5% decrease in product revenue from B2C segment to RMB223.2 million (US$31.9 million) in 2025 from RMB261.2 million in the prior year. Such decreases was primarily due to (i) enhanced competition in the pharmaceutical retail and wholesale industry in China; and (ii) our strategic transition towards an asset-light business model as we completed the divesture of several operating subsidiaries in the third quarter of 2025. These divested subsidiaries collectively contributed approximately 20.0% of our consolidated net revenue in 2024 and their combined net revenue for 2025 before the divesture decreased by 38.2% as compared to their combined revenue for 2024. See “Item 4. Information on the Company—A. History and Development of the Company” for details of our structural optimization.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Results of Operations","block":1061,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"b94a0d03b75373f3ea52385075882235442dca5525b23b1d26b43543bdf2d522","quote":"Service revenues. Our service revenues decreased by 19.8% from RMB106.5 million in 2024 to RMB85.4 million (US$12.2 million) in 2025, primarily due to the decrease of our B2B digital marketing service revenues in 2025.","context":"Product Revenues by Segment. Product revenues decreased by 12.8% from RMB14.3 billion in 2024 to RMB12.5 billion (US$1.8 billion) in 2025, as a result of (i) the 12.7% decrease in product revenue from B2B segment to RMB12.2 billion (US$1.7 billion) in 2025 from RMB14.0 billion in the prior year and (ii) the 14.5% decrease in product revenue from B2C segment to RMB223.2 million (US$31.9 million) in 2025 from RMB261.2 million in the prior year. Such decreases was primarily due to (i) enhanced competition in the pharmaceutical retail and wholesale industry in China; and (ii) our strategic transition towards an asset-light business model as we completed the divesture of several operating subsidiaries in the third quarter of 2025. These divested subsidiaries collectively contributed approximately 20.0% of our consolidated net revenue in 2024 and their combined net revenue for 2025 before the divesture decreased by 38.2% as compared to their combined revenue for 2024. See “Item 4. Information on the Company—A. History and Development of the Company” for details of our structural optimization.","section":"Results of Operations","block":1062,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"62686b1522576e508d99ff0ed18059f23c34cc58d91a79ad5206c8e7bac5ebb0","quote":"Cost of products sold decreased by 12.8% from RMB13.6 billion in 2024 to RMB11.8 billion (US$1.7 billion) in 2025, in line with our overall revenue decrease, which is primarily attributable to the decrease of sales in the B2B segment.","context":"Segment Cost of Products Sold","section":"Results of Operations","block":1064,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"56a06a4c12d479b4d4da521e934ed89bbf7a6b7b9ad0349283a6ceff7253630f","quote":"As a result of the foregoing, our segment profit from our B2C segment decreased by 31.1% from RMB63.7 million in 2024 to RMB43.9 million (US$6.3 million) in 2025 because of the decrease in our revenues from the B2C segment. Our segment profit from B2B segment decreased by 11.2% from RMB765.5 million in 2024 to RMB679.5 million (US$97.2 million) in 2025, and such decrease is also in line with the decrease in our revenues from the B2B segment.","context":"Segment Profit/Loss","section":"Results of Operations","block":1066,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.se