 to the decrease of sales in the B2B segment.","context":"Segment Cost of Products Sold","section":"Results of Operations","block":1084,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"daef3fd52d71e505d8b85d8af44c8129bb35bfe554616beeef5588e9f77c10de","quote":"As a result of the foregoing, our segment profit from our B2C segment decreased by 19.8% from RMB79.4 million in 2023 to RMB63.7 million in 2024 because of the decrease in our revenues from the B2C segment. Our segment profit from our B2B segment decreased by 0.5% from RMB769.6 million in 2023 to RMB765.5 million in 2024, and such decrease is also in line with the decrease in our revenues from the B2B segment.","context":"Segment Profit/Loss","section":"Results of Operations","block":1086,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"7b238fbd46928c6c10562179797425d8a82d2b3df25c115c6920713b7c789c00","quote":"The following table sets forth material amounts of cash and short-term investments disaggregated by currency denomination as of December 31, 2025 in each jurisdiction in which our affiliated entities are domiciled:","context":"We expect that substantially all of our future net revenues will be denominated in Renminbi. Under existing PRC foreign exchange regulations, payments of current account items, including profit distributions, interest payments and trade and service-related foreign exchange transactions, can be made in foreign currencies without prior SAFE approval as long as certain routine procedural requirements are fulfilled. Therefore, our PRC subsidiary, 1 Pharmacy Technology, is allowed to pay dividends in foreign currencies to us without prior SAFE approval by following certain routine procedural requirements. However, approval from or registration with competent government authorities is required where the Renminbi is to be converted into foreign currency and remitted out of China to pay capital expenses such as the repayment of loans denominated in foreign currencies. The PRC government may at its discretion restrict access to foreign currencies for current account transactions in the future.","section":"Results of Operations","block":1140,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"3ab47a923748c8d40ca52ed01bde994987285b8d0bb8b5553e9e6cd682826dcf","quote":"| | | | | | | ​ ​ ​ | PRC | ​ ​ ​ | Hong Kong | ​ ​ ​ | Cayman Islands | | (RMB in thousands) Cash and short-term investments in RMB | | 518,682 | | 142 | | 20,377 Cash and short-term investments in US$ | | — | | 1,134 | | 20,663","context":"The following table sets forth material amounts of cash and short-term investments disaggregated by currency denomination as of December 31, 2025 in each jurisdiction in which our affiliated entities are domiciled:","section":"Results of Operations","block":1141,"table":" |  |  |  |  |  | \n | ​ ​ ​ | PRC | ​ ​ ​ | Hong Kong | ​ ​ ​ | Cayman Islands\n |  | (RMB in thousands)\nCash and short-term investments in RMB |  | 518,682 |  | 142 |  | 20,377\nCash and short-term investments in US$ |  | — |  | 1,134 |  | 20,663","attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"e0a876483714ecc897bf090a788bb200ed3551e4681dd3803c6799549e5d00e7","quote":"As described in Note 2(l) and Note 13, the Company generated substantially all of its revenue from sales of medicines, healthcare products and other wellness merchandise through its online platforms in the year ended December 31, 2025, of which product revenues from the B2B segment (“B2B product sales”) were RMB12,247 million, or 97.5% of total revenues. The Company recognizes revenues from B2B product sales at the point in time when the delivery was completed and uses systems to process and record its revenue transactions.","context":"Revenue Recognition","section":"Item 19. Exhibits","block":1729,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"ebdcf088fdcc3c854cdf1d23fe37bf64d7047ec408dab3b92e819ded901fa51d","quote":"The principal considerations for our determination that occurrence of product revenue is a critical audit matter are the inherent risk around the occurrence of revenue given the significance of B2B product sales and large volume processed by the systems. Our audit procedures related to B2B product revenue recognition included the following, among others:","context":"As described in Note 2(l) and Note 13, the Company generated substantially all of its revenue from sales of medicines, healthcare products and other wellness merchandise through its online platforms in the year ended December 31, 2025, of which product revenues from the B2B segment (“B2B product sales”) were RMB12,247 million, or 97.5% of total revenues. The Company recognizes revenues from B2B product sales at the point in time when the delivery was completed and uses systems to process and record its revenue transactions.","section":"Item 19. Exhibits","block":1730,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"16c85ad2b2c7de4e0abb3fa0bb66e6e3150afe8f5ef8b0186c1a705ac73d4017","quote":"In accordance with ASC 280, Segment Reporting, the Group’s chief operating decision maker (the “CODM”) has been identified as the Co-Chairmen and Chief Executive Officer, who reviews the segment information when making decisions about allocating resources and assessing performance of the Group. The Group classifies its operations into two segments: B2C segment and B2B segment whereby the B2C business represents revenue generated from individual consumers while B2B business represents revenue generated from corporate customers. There are no internal revenue transactions between the reportable segments. The Group does not distinguish expenses (i.e. operating expenses and other expenses) between segments in its internal reporting, and reports expenses by nature as a whole. For segment reporting purposes, the Group’s CODM evaluates segment performance based on segment profit. Cost of product sold is the only significant expense regularly provided to the CODM and included in the measurement of segment profit. Operating expenses and other expenses are managed and reviewed on a consolidated basis only and are not allocated to individual segments.","context":"(ac) Segment reporting","section":"Item 19. Exhibits","block":2034,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"31d92285bf934bb36231e24106b63aa2f65663b20cce29a346b8affa87a86a62","quote":"As a result, the Group does not allocate or disclose certain expense details by segment. Furthermore, the Group’s CODM is not provided with asset information by segment. As such, no asset information by segment is presented. The information of segment reporting is presented consistently for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025. The following tables summarize the Group’s product revenues and segment profit generated by its segments.","context":"In accordance with ASC 280, Segment Reporting, the Group’s chief operating decision maker (the “CODM”) has been identified as the Co-Chairmen and Chief Executive Officer, who reviews the segment information when making decisions about allocating resources and assessing performance of the Group. The Group classifies its operations into two segments: B2C segment and B2B segment whereby the B2C business represents revenue generated from individual consumers while B2B business represents revenue generated from corporate customers. There are no internal revenue transactions between the reportable segments. The Group does not distinguish expenses (i.e. operating expenses and other expenses) between segments in its internal reporting, and reports expenses by nature as a whole. For segment reporting purposes, the Group’s CODM evaluates segment performance based on segment profit. Cost of product sold is the only significant expense regularly provided to the CODM and included in the measurement of segment profit. Operating expenses and other expenses are managed and reviewed on a consolidated basis only and are not allocated to individual segments.","section":"Item 19. Exhibits","block":2035,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001104659-26-052002","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-30","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001738906","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1738906/000110465926052002/yi-20251231x20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f.bin","sha256":"786074c9b9ae6fe909ee8723345810fa662ab7359b8463aa269fb0edc8c1389f"}},{"id":"3afd4c12be025e4f8d3f91a3fe85b6646564b17752e2f41eae655fc54a78bef9","quote":"| | | | | | | | Years Ended December 31, | ​ ​ ​ | 2023 | ​ ​ ​ | 2024 | ​ ​ ​ | 2025 B2C segment | | ​ | | ​ | | ​ Product revenues | | 357,975 | | 261,197 | | 223,217 Service revenues | | 19,388 | | 16,900 | | 11,601 Cost of products sold* | | (297,979) | | (21